<title>USA: Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Nov 1-3.</title>
<headline>Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Nov 1-3.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data</p>
<p>for the top 10 movies at the November 1-3 U.S. box office,</p>
<p>according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Romeo and Juliet	 $11,133,231	    ----</p>
<p>2. Sleepers		    $8,039,085	 $ 37,572,441</p>
<p>3. High School High	  $5,009,703	 $ 12,610,968</p>
<p>4. Larger Than Life	  $3,779,504	 $  ----</p>
<p>5. The Ghost and the</p>
<p>   Darkness		    $3,660,201	 $ 31,779,391</p>
<p>6. Stephen King's Thinner  $3,582,333	 $ 10,877,181</p>
<p>7. The First Wives Club    $3,561,788	 $ 93,741,105</p>
<p>8. Dear God		    $3,213,045	 $  ----</p>
<p>9. The Associate	     $3,118,515	 $  8,664,334</p>
<p>10 The Long Kiss Goodnight $2,377,892	 $ 28,917,473</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; is released</p>
<p>by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;Sleepers&quot; is released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros. &quot;High School High&quot; is released by Sony Corp's TriStar Pictures. &quot;Larger Than Life&quot; is released by MGM, which is owned by financier Kirk Kerkorian and Seven Network Ltd . &quot;The Ghost and the Darkness&quot;, &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; &quot;Stephen King's Thinner&quot; and &quot;Dear God&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;The Associate&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;The Long Kiss Goodnight&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner's Turner Broadcasting System.</p>
</text>
